
Implement reliable deferred INVOCATION context cleanup
for the existing TestNG lifecycle integration.

The current implementation relies on counting
declared @AfterMethod methods, which fails when
configuration methods are filtered or disabled.

Requirements:

1. Do not determine invocation completion by counting
   declared teardown methods.

2. Keep the INVOCATION context available throughout
   @BeforeMethod, @Test, managed test-result callbacks,
   and all applicable @AfterMethod callbacks.

3. Release the previous invocation when the next
   distinct logical test invocation begins.

4. When a TestNG scope finishes, release any remaining
   invocation contexts, even if no subsequent test runs.

5. Cleanup must work with parallel DataProviders,
   retries, skipped tests and filtered configuration
   methods.

6. Do not rely solely on ThreadLocal for final cleanup.
   Contexts must be tracked by stable identifiers.

7. Never release a context while it has an active
   managed activation.

8. Preserve the current configuration inheritance
   and override behavior.

9. Reuse existing lifecycle components.
   Do not introduce unnecessary abstractions.

10. Keep all TestNG-specific code outside core.

